# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R3; the
# completeness critic's correction, *a move that changes what a bound name
# means says so*).
#
# `fixedbugs-563-width.h` spells `Wide`, which `fixedbugs-563-wide.h`
# defines, so the first group is refused and the move that compiles is the
# second group above it. Both headers define `FIXEDBUGS_563_WIDTH` only where
# nothing has, 8 and 16, so moving the second above the first makes `width`
# add 16 where the groups as written would add 8. Both orders are
# preprocessed once, and the note names `width`, whose definition reads
# otherwise.
extern "fixedbugs-563-width.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function width(w: Wide) -> i32

extern "fixedbugs-563-wide.h"
    record Wide
        v: i32

function main()
    print(width(w: Wide(v: 1)))
